// @expect-error A 'char' is a code point and never converts to 'float' on its own. Write 'letter as float' to use its code point as a 'float'.
// The narrower floating-point type is refused for the same reason as the wider one, and a 'char'
// variable is refused exactly as a literal is.
main() -> int {
    char letter = 'A';
    float code = letter;
    return code > 0.0 ? 0 : 1;
}
